From 9f80b4db79677cb97c288b96349768ad1d5f95bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Iuri Jikidze <37273763+ijiki16@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:14:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/39] arm64: dts: allwinner: a733: match GMAC0 reset roles to
 the vendor BSP

stmmac pulses its "stmmaceth" reset (assert + deassert) during probe and
only deasserts the shared "ahb" one. With "stmmaceth" bound to
RST_BUS_GMAC0 the GMAC bus reset is pulsed after the glue has programmed
its syscfg register, wiping the RGMII/delay setup back to its reset
value 0x8000 (PHY_SEL = internal EPHY).

Bind "stmmaceth" to RST_BUS_GMAC0_AXI and "ahb" to RST_BUS_GMAC0, the
roles the vendor BSP (sun60iw2p1.dtsi, dwmac-sunxi) uses, so the glue can
release the bus reset itself (as a shared consumer) before programming
syscfg, and stmmac only pulses the AXI reset.

Verified on an OrangePi 4 Pro together with the following dwmac-sun60i
change: syscfg reads back 0x00011145, the same as under the vendor 6.6
kernel.

This change was made with the help of an AI coding assistant (Claude);
the analysis compared register dumps between the vendor and mainline
kernels on the board.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
index f24d81d50..6c7c3fe78 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun60i-a733.dtsi
@@ -437,8 +437,8 @@ gmac0: ethernet@4500000 {
 				 <&ccu CLK_GMAC0_PHY>,
 				 <&ccu CLK_GMAC_PTP>;
 			clock-names = "stmmaceth", "mbus", "phy", "ptp_ref";
-			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_GMAC0>,
-				 <&ccu RST_BUS_GMAC0_AXI>;
+			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_GMAC0_AXI>,
+				 <&ccu RST_BUS_GMAC0>;
 			reset-names = "stmmaceth", "ahb";
 			phy-mode = "rgmii";
 			pinctrl-names = "default";
